{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>You shall not eat any carcass.</b> Even from a clean species." "<b>For you are a holy people to HaShem your Elohim.</b> Even though the carcass is suitable as human food, as for a stranger or a foreigner, it is not suitable as food for a holy people prepared for the perfection intended by El, blessed be He." "<b>You shall not boil a kid.</b> Like the practice of the Canaanites, who thought by this act to increase their livestock, their possessions, and all their cattle."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:25.461698605Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}